<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#SacredRhythm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A tradition-specific ritual drumming pattern with defined entity associations, ceremonial function, and authority requirements for performance. In Lucumí: a toque or canto. In Haitian Vodou: a tanbou rhythm for a specific lwa. In Candomblé: a xirê toque. Each rhythm is identified by its name, entity association, tradition, and lineage variant. Rhythm names are community-restricted; possession-trigger status and toque sequences are initiated-only."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#authorityRequirement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "authority requirement"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#entityCalled> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-community-only> .
