<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#SacredInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A musical instrument used in Afro-Atlantic sacred contexts, which may be consecrated, named, or otherwise distinguished from secular instruments of the same type. Examples: a set of consecrated bàtá drums; Vodou rada drums (manman, seconde, bula); Candomblé rum/rumpi/lé. An instrument may have its own name, lineage, and history. The instrument type is public; consecration status and internal names are community-restricted."@en .
