<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#family-lucumi-bata> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Rhythms performed on the consecrated Añá bàtá drum set in Lucumí/Ocha tradition. Requires Olubatá authority and Aña initiation to lead. Considered the highest-authority drumming tradition in Lucumí; specific toques are associated with specific Orisha and are operationally significant."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#transmissionLineage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-ngoma> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#inst-shekere> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gourd rattle with bead netting used across Yorùbá-derived and related traditions. Consecrated shekeré are used in Orisha ceremonies; güiro refers to the Cuban variant."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#song-other> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-ngoma> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-framework/> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#instrumentName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The name of this specific consecrated instrument or set. For Añá bàtá: the name of the drum set. Community-restricted."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#family-candomble-angola> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
